From bd2fb145817f45b6396fa87bbbaea2f517ea49ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 10:34:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 01/17] port 823ed5e6, 630b7606: conversation cache: parked K/V
 segments and checkpoint state can be mapped one by one, so an eviction
 returns its RAM to the kernel (opt-in STRATA_CONV_MMAP=1, #3115)

Squash of 823ed5e6 and its fixup 630b7606 (the SYCL snapshot test reads the spare row into ConversationBytes).

Parked conversations (ConversationBuffer segments, ConversationCheckpoint gdn / ple / tails / dead / block_pos)
come from malloc, and glibc keeps what an eviction frees in its arenas, so the physical-RAM gate's next reading
does not move.  STRATA_CONV_MMAP=1 (read once): conversation_alloc.hpp's ConversationAllocator maps every
allocation of at least 64 KiB on its own and munmaps it on free; smaller ones and the switch unset go through
operator new exactly as std::allocator does.

Adaptations to v0.2.12:
- conversation_buffer.hpp: upstream's DefaultInit allocator (value-initializes only when asked, for
  resize_for_overwrite / STRATA_PARK_ASYNC) is replaced by ConversationAllocator<uint8_t, false>, which has the
  same construct() semantics.  The "fresh mapping is zero, skip the fill" rule sits in resize_impl's
  value != nullptr branch; resize_for_overwrite (value == nullptr) leaves the bytes alone as before.
  segment_capacity wraps its results in conversation_alloc_capacity (identity with the switch off).
- conversation_cache.hpp: only the evict_oldest comment changes; upstream's guarded-donor loop stays as is.
- generate.cpp: the RAM-gate comment re-placed by function; the "STRATA_CONV_MMAP: ..." startup line now sits
  after upstream's ParkSource struct (our base had it beside our park-capture setup, not ported yet).
- CMakeLists.txt: only conversation_alloc_test (+ _off) is registered; conversation_tier_test belongs to
  STRATA_CONV_TIER_DIR (a later group) and is not part of this port.
- conversation_tier_test.cpp is not added (does not exist in v0.2.12).

Without the variable the engine allocates as before (the checkpoint vectors' type changed; their behaviour did not).

(cherry picked from commit 823ed5e6ffd627f81d07b2f7527f06678744fcd2)
(cherry picked from commit 630b760697d90b8eaaf5ef2c29cb3d38293990a1)

